      "side": 1,
      "message": "This condition works in Linux mainstream but does not work in Android Common Kernel 5.4, thus it shall be modified as below instead:\n\nif (ufshcd_hba_is_crypto_supported(hba))\n\nThis is because UFSHCD_CAP_CRYPTO would be disabled by below call stack:\n\nufshcd_hba_enable() -\u003e\nufshcd_hba_stop() -\u003e\nufshcd_crypto_disable() -\u003e\nufshcd_crypto_disable_spec()\n\nAnd then,\n\nufshcd_vops_hce_enable_notify() -\u003e\nufs_mtk_hce_enable_notify() will not see UFSHCD_CAP_CRYPTO in hba-\u003ecaps, so finally Crypto feature in MediaTek platform will not be enabled.\n\nExcept for above essential modification, others are fine and have been tested by ourselves.\n\nThanks Eric for the backport.",
